Subject: [PATCH] virtual: retain buffer iteration across request completion

The final buffer completion can release the request on the consumer thread.
Snapshot its buffer map before emitting completion, so advancing the last
iterator does not dereference a destroyed Request. This maintained downstream
fix preserves the original31 FP6 patches unchanged. Derived from libcamera
191e202178f02430b5942397c70d215cdd2056fa; upstream LGPL-2.1-or-later.
Observed baseline: full upstream multi_stream_test SIGSEGV11 at virtual.cpp133.
With the fix: all 4 GStreamer tests pass over 10 repetitions.
No hardware qualification is implied.

--- a/src/libcamera/pipeline/virtual/virtual.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/pipeline/virtual/virtual.cpp
@@ -130,7 +130,8 @@
 
 void VirtualCameraData::processRequest(Request *request)
 {
-	for (const auto &[stream, buffer] : request->buffers()) {
+	const auto buffers = request->buffers();
+	for (const auto &[stream, buffer] : buffers) {
 		bool found = false;
 		/* map buffer and fill test patterns */
 		for (auto &streamConfig : streamConfigs_) {
